review:
trash
had a game breaking but after the first hour. restarted anew and had the same but again. 
@at dev. its the mushroomquest who wants a lute. insted of dropping the lute on the counter it always lands in the stash first but the mushroom sees it as being on the counter and doesent accept the real lute. we finnish the deal, i dont get the gold and the next customer is the mushroom again with the same quest already saying that there is a lute on the counter-> permalocked

////Read Update below////

Initially I pre-purchased this before the original release date. I was disappointed when a week later it still wasn't released so I requested a refund. Recently it went on sale so I took a chance. I read a lot of the early reviews, wasn't too impressed with what I was reading. I thought that since it's been out about a year now, the reviews started looking better so since it was on sale I'd give it a try. I had issues at first with constant crashes, since the latest update has come out it seems the issues have been resolved and I have been enjoying the game play. I believe part of my initial issues was that I originally installed it on a HDD. Since I've uninstalled it and reinstalled it on a SSD that has helped tremendously. I'm happy that I didn't have to ask for a second refund.

////UPDATE////
I don't know what they did but the game crashes all the dam time now. If I'm lucky i can play 1 game then it crashes, Don't be mistaken by my hours played as some of them hours are due to trying to get the dam game to run. Some of them are also hours that the game kept running after submitting a crash report and the game not stopping on it's own like it is supposed to do. This has really been annoying.

One of the buggiest games I've played that costs $30 and ISN'T in Early Access. Save your money. I hope negative reviews don't sway them from fixing the abundance of issues* but I cannot in good faith recommend this game for the current price and the current way the game plays with how terrible the optimization** is. Just play Medieval Dynasty instead.


*(Raids unable to finish because the enemy falls under the map and gets stuck there;

the custom/cheat menu not working;

enemies appearing downed but still moving & attacking like normal with an empty riposte bar;

enemies completely ignoring your block and damaging you through it without breaking you or your block/riposte down;

one of the side quests required you to get meat from animals but the animals were invincible from all damage;

villagers not using the tools assigned to them, not using their station to produce anything despite having all required resources, or just outright not working at all and wandering around;

buildings unable to be built or moved, having to spam click or try multiple times for the game to register that they can in fact be built and when trying to move them it thinks I am pressing the key to change the material/type instead of wanting to move it;

multiple blueprints can only be unlocked by building said blueprint which, obviously, you can't do without cheating (for example: The Stonemason Station, Miner's Workplace & all of the Segmented Fences);

enemy weapons appearing invisible & their attack animations not playing, making it near impossible to block or parry;

sometimes the game randomly makes you take fall damage. you can fall down a, not even 1 foot- hell not even .5 foot- fall and take half your health bar in damage;

just to name a few...)

**(The optimization is terrible, I'm not sure if its a memory leak or what but having an 11 population village is causing my frames to drop down to the 40s (capped at 120 normally, monitor refresh rate), my CPU usage to shoot up from normally a 50-65% to a near 100% at 86-98% and temps to go from a normal 65-75 C to 85-90 C where I basically have to stay far away from my village if I don't want to risk my PC overheating with fresh thermal paste (3 months) and a new CPU/cooling. Larger NPC villages are about the same, even on lowest possible settings (which is why I haven't mentioned the world not loading textures in frequently, not sure if thats just poor optimization again or because of the low settings). The only thing I haven't experienced from what other reviews have said are the crashes, but maybe I just haven't seen a large enough village to have that happen yet, but with how its going with just 11 (10) NPCs I wouldn't be surprised if I do end up crashing by the time I get 20 villagers.)

TL;DR It was enjoyable for the first few hours but became near unplayable due to bugs and poor optimization.
